Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.50,0:00:06.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,What's worth replicating — and has anyone checked it?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.00,0:00:14.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,Ranked off the OpenAIRE Graph: impact, momentum,\Nand whether the materials to re-run it exist.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.00,0:00:19.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,It overlays what the Graph can't:\Nwhich claims were independently checked.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.00,0:00:32.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,Open one — the signed Science Live nanopublication:\Nthe outcome and its evidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.00,0:00:43.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,High-impact, but no linked materials —\Nso it can't be re-run.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.00,0:00:53.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,This one's reproducible: code and data linked,\Narchived in Software Heritage.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.50,0:01:00.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,A live FAIR-software read, plus RSE practices —\Ndocumented, tested, CI.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.00,0:01:07.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,Hit Replicate — the FORRT template\Nruns on the replication-radar MCP.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.00,0:01:14.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,So we switch to the agent —\Nsame engine, now an MCP.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.00,0:01:33.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,The agent asks the Radar what's un-replicated:\NOliver 2018 — 1,700 citations, never checked.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.00,0:02:03.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,It finds independent software — XMHW —\Nand catches one that only looks independent.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.00,0:02:24.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,It hands off to the OpenAIRE MCP for independent\Ndata — a true replication, not a re-run.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.00,0:02:38.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,Honest scope: the satellite era only;\Nthe century-long trend stays open.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.50,0:02:45.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,It creates the repo and records\Nthe paper, data, and software.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.50,0:02:49.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,Two MCPs on one Graph — discover, then check.\NReplication Radar.
